                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Draft Cable to SCAP </hi>
                </p>
                <p> FEC Weekly Summary of Information on Japanese Economic and Financial Affairs
                    C2–026/42 15 October 1947 contains quote attributed to Sebald 30 September 1947
                    before Allied Council for Japan that FEC decision to set Japan’s post-war
                    industrial level at 1930–34 too low because of alleged failure to allow for
                    population increase. This is based upon misapprehension. FEC policy decision as
                    well as levels of industry now under FEC consideration take into account
                    population increase. Request that correction be made upon suitable
                    opportunity.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
